        "slideId": "s11",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Stripping names and Social Security Numbers never guarantees anonymity. Latanya Sweeney famously proved that eighty-seven percent of the US population is uniquely identified by just three quasi-identifiers: five-digit ZIP code, gender, and exact birth date.",
