        "slideId": "s9",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Case Study 3 is ProPublica's 2016 audit of COMPAS criminal recidivism scoring. COMPAS achieved Predictive Parity—around 60 percent re-arrest calibration regardless of race. Yet because base re-arrest rates differed, COMPAS severely violated Equalized Odds: Black non-reoffenders were mislabeled High Risk at 44.9 percent versus 23.5 percent for white non-reoffenders, while white re-offenders were mislabeled Low Risk nearly twice as often.",
