        "slideId": "s10",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "That is the dreaded JSON object overhead, Kaito. Every single key and value is instantiated as an independent heap object with its own ref-count, pointer metadata, and memory padding. Arrow completely eliminates that.",
